{{also|Ray|rày|rây|rầy|ra'y|-raþ}}
==English==
[[Image:Crepuscular rays with clouds and high contrast fg FL.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Rays from the [[sun]] (1)]]
{{wikipedia|mul=ray (fish)}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|rā}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹeɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ray.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪ|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Via {{inh|en|enm|-}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|rai}}, from {{der|en|la|radius||staff, stake, spoke}}. {{doublet|en|radius}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[beam]] of light or [[radiation]].
#: {{ux|en|I saw a '''ray''' of light through the clouds.}}
#* {{RQ:Eddison Worm|5|Strangely light and delicate was his frame and seeming, yet with a sense of slumbering power beneath, as the delicate peak of a snow mountain seen afar in the low red '''rays''' of morning.}}
# {{lb|en|zoology}} A [[rib]]-like [[reinforcement]] of [[bone]] or [[cartilage]] in a fish's [[fin]].
# {{lb|en|zoology}} One of the [[spheromere]]s of a [[radiate]], especially one of the arms of a [[starfish]] or an [[ophiuran]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} A radiating part of a flower or plant; the [[marginal]] [[floret]]s of a compound flower, such as an [[aster]] or a [[sunflower]]; one of the [[pedicel]]s of an [[umbel]] or other circular flower cluster; [[radius]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Sight; perception; vision; from an old theory of vision, that sight was something which proceeded from the eye to the object seen.
#* {{RQ:Pope Dunciad|passage=All eyes direct their '''rays''' / On him, and crowds turn coxcombs as they gaze.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A line extending indefinitely in one direction from a point.

